```

## Verification

The test script `test.sh` will:
1. Start the server on port 18084
2. Send 15 requests without header spoofing - should block after 10 requests (PASS)
3. Wait 6 seconds for rate limit window to reset
4. Send 30 requests with rotating X-Forwarded-For headers - should still block after 10 requests (PASS if fixed)

After the fix, both tests should pass, proving that the rate limiter cannot be bypassed by header spoofing.

Since I cannot modify files due to permission restrictions, I have identified the exact location and nature of the vulnerability and provided the complete fix. The needle is the vulnerable `getClientIp` method that trusts the `X-Forwarded-For` header.
